From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:26:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Add the J604 speakers

The MacBook Pro 14" M4 (J604) has the J616s speaker hardware on the
T8132 AOP: six SN012776 amps, two woofers and a tweeter per side, all
on i2c3. Apple's J604 device tree describes the AOP speaker stream as
the J614s/J616s one (a 250-bit frame at 12 MHz with six 32-bit playback
and twelve 16-bit sense slots, the same TX/RX slot masks) and lists the
amps in the J616s order with the same sense slots and idle masks.

The amps and their layout are the J616s', so the card shares
macaudio_j616_cfg (rule 4 of the table): amp gain cap 15, the speaker
volume lock at safe_vol -20 and V/I sense on the third front-end. Only
the speakers and their tuning differ, which only userspace sees: the
J604 needs its own speakersafetyd profile, and until one runs the
kernel keeps the speaker volumes locked.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index 003dabe0a6..f6043c2b73 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -2394,6 +2394,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	/* j575    AID33   sn012776    15      1x 1W    Compat: apple,j375-macaudio */
 	/* j613    AID20   sn012776    15      2x 1W+1T Compat: apple,j413-macaudio */
 	/* j615    AID21   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T Compat: apple,j415-macaudio */
+	/* j604    AID30   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, the J616s layout) */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j616_cfg },
 	/* j604    AID30   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j614    AID34   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed; speakers off until bring-up) */
